The cash‑flows are the annual coupons of 4 and the principal of 100 at year 5.  
Discount each cash‑flow with the appropriate spot rate (annual compounding):

\[
\begin{aligned}
P &=\frac{4}{(1+0.03)^1}
   +\frac{4}{(1+0.032)^2}
   +\frac{4}{(1+0.035)^3}
   +\frac{4}{(1+0.038)^4}
   +\frac{4+100}{(1+0.04)^5} \\[4pt]
  &=\frac{4}{1.03}
   +\frac{4}{1.032^{2}}
   +\frac{4}{1.035^{3}}
   +\frac{4}{1.038^{4}}
   +\frac{104}{1.04^{5}} \\[4pt]
  &\approx 3.8835 + 3.7558 + 3.6080 + 3.4456 + 3.2877 + 82.1927 \\[4pt]
  &\approx 100.17 .
\end{aligned}
\]

\[
\boxed{\text{Bond price } \approx 100.17}
\]

ANSWER: 100.17

